    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the difference between an absolute date and a relative date?\n\nOptions: \nA. An absolute date is a fixed point in time, while a relative date is flexible and can be adjusted according to context.\nB. A relative date is derived from radiometric dating techniques, while an absolute date is only associated with written documents.\nC. An absolute date is based on the Gregorian calendar, while a relative date is based on lunar phases.\nD. A relative date refers to a year or a range of years, while an absolute date indicates a chronological order.\nE. A relative date is a date that can be calculated from an absolute date, while an absolute date cannot be derived from a relative date.\nF. A relative date is an exact moment in time, while an absolute date is a general time period.\nG. An absolute date is known by everyone, while a relative date ranges from 30 to 50 years.\nH. An absolute date refers to a year or a range of years, while a relative date indicates a chronological order.\nI. A relative date is determined using carbon dating, while an absolute date is estimated using historical records.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
