hat Ghanians were engaged, directly or indirectly, in trade with Asia?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Ghanian king had adopted the Chinese tradition of the kow-tow .\nB. The Ghanians grew vegetables, which may have been Asian in origin.\nC. They kept horses in their court, which would have come from the Mongols.\nD. The king collected nuggets from mines, possibly hinting at trade relations with Asian miners.\nE. The people paid taxes in gold, indicating wealth from trade.\nF. The king adorned himself with gold and jewels, probably from India.\nG. The people in his court wore silk robes.\nH. The Ghanians had wells with sweet water, possibly influenced by Asian irrigation techniques.\nI. The king's ministers were Muslims, suggesting trade with the Middle East.\nJ. The king wore necklaces and bracelets, possibly made of Asian materials.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
