    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4743",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\nRead the following excerpt.\nNever were talents of the highest genius of the most exalted kind, more profusely bestowed upon a human being. The genius of Napoleon is astounding. All branches of human knowledge seemed alike familiar to his gigantic mind. His conversations at St. Helena, scattered through the numerous and voluminous memorials of those who gleaned them, are replete with intensest interest. During the long agony of his imprisonment and his death, he conversed with perfect freedom upon the events of his marvelous career, and upon all those subjects or morals, politics, and religion, which most deeply concern the welfare of our race. There is no mind which will not be invigorated by familiarity with these profound thoughts, expressed with so much glow of feeling and energy of diction.\n—John S. C. Abbott, historian, Napoleon at St. Helena, 1855\nWhich of the following features of the French empire under Napoleon does Abbott seem most impressed with?\n\nOptions: \nA. Napoleon's domestic reforms\nB. Napoleon's economic policies\nC. Napoleon's military tactics\nD. Napoleon's approach to religion\nE. Napoleon's secret police\nF. Napoleon's treatment of prisoners\nG. Napoleon's diplomatic strategies\nH. Napoleon's suppression of women's rights\nI. Napoleon's expansionist strategies\nJ. Napoleon's influence on art and culture\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The excerpt emphasizes Napoleon's profound thoughts on morals, politics, and religion, highlighting his intellectual and cultural influence rather than specific policies or military actions. Abbott is most impressed with Napoleon's broad knowledge and the depth of his conversations, which align with his impact on art and culture. Therefore, the correct answer is J.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 350,
        "output_tokens": 516,
        "total_tokens": 866
      },
      "provider": "apiyi",
      "error": null
